# ---------------------------------------------------------------- drought (bad, cycle A)

== the year it did not rain
tier: life event
land: drought
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 12-90
per_year: 0 0 0 0 0 0
when: a dry year: field and water stretches lose health
tone: trouble
life: nature, home
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, rival, friend
earth: a summer without rain, the reservoir low, and a ban on garden hoses
tribal: a dry season, the springs failing one by one, and the herds walked further each day for water
magic: a dry year, the tower's well dropping a rung a week, and the valley's fields cracking open
scene: It has not rained properly since spring. The reservoir is a ring of cracked mud, the council has banned hosepipes, and {Ns} garden is wilting by the day.
scene W: Most of the street is keeping to the ban. {rival}, two doors down, plainly is not.
scene U: The downpipe from the roof runs into nothing, and {N} has been thinking about that.
scene B: A farmer up the valley is selling a share of water rights cheaply, because nobody thinks it will matter.
scene R: The beans will be dead by the weekend, and nobody checks gardens at night.
scene G: The lawn is turning the colour of straw, and {N} is not sure it matters.
scene tribal: The springs are failing one by one, and the herds walk further for water every day. The elders talk late into the night about where to move the camp.
scene magic: The tower's well drops a rung a week, and the valley's fields are cracking open. The water masters have set a rule on every bucket.
