tribal: a hard frost after the sowing moon, and the new shoots in the clearing dead by sunrise
magic: a late frost off the mountain, and the herb beds below the tower killed overnight
scene: The forecast said mild, and the night came clear and still. In the morning {N} goes out to find the beans, the tomatoes and the early potatoes all limp and spoiled with frost.
scene W: Next door's beds are uncovered too, and {neighbour} is away until the weekend.
scene U: {N} has a notebook of last-frost dates going back years, and this one is late, even by those.
scene B: The garden centre still has trays of young plants, at a price.
scene R: There are seeds left in the packets, and the whole day ahead.
scene G: It happens, {parent} always said. Some years the frost has the last word.
scene tribal: A hard frost came after the sowing moon, and the new shoots in the clearing are dead by sunrise. The planters stand looking at the ground, saying nothing.
scene magic: A late frost came down off the mountain and killed the herb beds below the tower overnight. The gardener-master is already muttering at the stars.
